---
// Three things you can run today (2026-11-07, for KubeCon NA): the AI Cluster Runtime stack on kind,
// the agent in the cluster with kagent, and the gh-aw pipeline — the marquee examples, each a public
// repository. The copy lives in data/examples.ts, shared with /demo/, the hub that carries each one's
// visual; the band's one visual is the kagent figure (PipelineFigure renders on /use-cases/ and /demo/,
// the AICR stills in the Engine band and on /demo/; one SVG figure per page). The home page's marks
// note sits here, under the last band that names a third party, and covers UseCasesTeaser's names too.
import { examples } from '../data/examples';
import KagentFigure from './figures/KagentFigure.astro';
---

<section class="band alt" id="examples">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head">
      <h2>Three things you can run today.</h2>
      <p>Each is a public repository and a README. The first two run on kind, on a laptop with Docker;
        the third runs in your GitHub organization.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="figwide">
      <KagentFigure />
      <p class="figcap"><b>The agent in the cluster.</b> A person approves in the kagent UI; the agent
        calls Turf through the egress gateway, which adds the token; the engine runs only while there
        is work; the state never leaves the cluster.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="solutions">
      {examples.map((ex) => (
        <div class="sol">
          <span class="tagline">{ex.tagline}</span>
          <h3>{ex.title}</h3>
          <p>{ex.blurb}</p>
          <p class="links">{ex.links.map((l) => <a href={l.href}>{l.label} →</a>)}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="also">More, with each example’s walkthrough and two recordings from before 1.0 →
      <a href="/demo/">turf.build/demo</a></p>
    <p class="legal-note">NVIDIA, AI Cluster Runtime, NVCRE, NVSentinel, KAI Scheduler and NIM are trademarks or
      product names of NVIDIA Corporation, referred to here only to describe interoperability. Amazon EKS,
      Google Kubernetes Engine and Azure Kubernetes Service are trademarks of their respective owners. MAAS
      is a trademark of Canonical Ltd. Redfish is a trademark of DMTF. Amazon Web Services and AWS are
      trademarks of Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. GitHub and GitHub Agentic Workflows are trademarks
      of GitHub, Inc. kagent, gVisor and Knative are trademarks or project names of their respective owners.
      Restate is a product of Restate Software, Inc. and Restate GmbH, named here to describe what Turf is
      built on. Turf is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any of them. All other marks
      belong to their owners.</p>
  </div>
</section>
